{
  "requirement": "Evidence inputs MAY have a definition form containing exactly `definition` and `text`. `definition` MUST identify one named definition; `text` MUST contain its complete raw fenced declaration as source lines, including its phrase option and explanatory body.\n\nValidation MUST reject missing definitions and changed snapshot text, identifying the definition and showing a compact diff when available. Moving an unchanged definition within its chapter MUST NOT invalidate its snapshot. Evidence displays MUST show the definition name, current source location, and recorded text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: the requirement is satisfied.** The implementation covers each obligation, it is marked `{impl}`, and tests exercise the main cases and failure modes. I found no unmarked implementing code and no acknowledged FIXME gaps.\n\n**Implementation**\n- **Definition form.** `validate_input` in `src/evidence.rs` takes the definition branch when a `definition` key is present.\n  - `check_keys([\"definition\",\"text\"])` enforces the \"exactly `definition` and `text`\" shape and rejects any other field.\n  - `string_field` requires `definition` to be a string.\n  - `text_field` requires `text` to be a nonempty array of strings.\n- **One named definition.** `InputSelector::Definition` in `src/inputs.rs` resolves through `definitions.get(name)` filtered to `DefinitionKind::Term`. Otherwise it returns `\"{definition}: no matching named definition\"`.\n- **Complete raw declaration.** Resolution returns the term's `raw_lines`, redacted via `redaction::redact_lines`. Redaction is covered by `requirements.authoring.redaction`, which the code also marks. `to_input` records `{definition, text}`, and `from_input` parses that form.\n- **Rejecting missing definitions.** A definition that no longer resolves produces a labelled error that names it, for example `inputs[0]: rules.gone: no matching named definition`.\n- **Rejecting changed text.** `validate_resolved_input` compares the recorded text with the freshly resolved text. On a mismatch it reports `input text changed for Definition { definition: … }` followed by `compact_diff` output.\n  - The diff keeps only the changed lines, marked `-` and `+`, and truncates runs longer than eight lines.\n- **Moving a definition.** The snapshot holds only the raw declaration lines, with no line numbers or file offsets. Moving an unchanged definition therefore leaves the comparison unchanged.\n- **Displays.**\n  - `render_input` in `src/index.rs` labels the input `definition <name>`, so the name appears even when resolution fails.\n  - It shows each resolved range through `render_source_location`, giving the name and current `file:start–end`.\n  - It then shows the recorded text, falling back to the recorded text when the selector is unresolved.\n  - `InputLocation::resolve` supplies the current location.\n- **Marking.** The functions that carry out the requirement all carry `{impl}`: `validate_input`, `validate_resolved_input`, `from_input`, `to_input`, `InputSelector::resolve`, `InputLocation::resolve` and `render_input`.\n  - Other code that builds or reads definition inputs implements different requirements and is marked for those: `update_inputs` (capture), the authoring tools (`authoring_inputs`), and `validate_dependencies` (dependencies).\n\n**Tests**\n- **Display.** `index::detail_page_shows_recorded_text_locations_and_first_matching_group` checks four things:\n  - the definition label appears;\n  - the location line `md/rules.md:9–13` appears;\n  - the recorded text appears (not the current text);\n  - the ordering is correct.\n- **Capture, move, and missing or duplicate inputs.** `tests/definitions.rs::cyclic_dependencies_are_captured_once_and_changes_require_review` captures the three inputs and checks that validation passes. It then prepends blank lines to the chapter, which moves the definitions, and validation still passes. Next it changes a phrase option and a body line, and each change is reported as `input text changed`, naming the `glossary.*` definition. It also checks the missing and duplicate definition-input counts.\n- **Compact diff and `text` schema.** `changed_definition_snapshots_show_a_compact_diff_and_text_is_required` asserts that the diff is exactly one `-` line and one `+` line. It also checks that a missing, empty, or non-array `text` is rejected.\n- **Missing definition and extra field.** `definition_schema_deletion_and_literal_references_are_checked` checks that an unexpected field is rejected. It also checks that deleting the glossary file yields `glossary.a … no matching named definition`.\n- **Schema variants.** `evidence::schema_rejects_each_malformed_field_and_input_form` and `configuration_and_dependency_failures_do_not_stop_later_checks` cover non-string definitions, an empty `text`, mixed definition and requirements keys, and an unresolvable definition.",
  "references": "5f27461ed46183dca8e240ed4e7780d7ea9614bfaabbece36921a4b4d7fbba30",
